From cde97ecda32b4782f3bb4d1dc08c836be03eb03f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iuri Jikidze <37273763+ijiki16@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:14:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/39] clk: a733 bringup: print clock gate traces with
 pr_debug

The bringup trace hook clk_pcie_watch() printed every clock
enable/disable at KERN_EMERG. Once mmc0 runs with broken-cd (polled card
detect), that is several lines per second on the serial console, which
"dmesg -n" cannot silence and which makes the console unusable as a
shell. Use pr_debug so the traces are still available through dynamic
debug.

Tested on an OrangePi 4 Pro: the console is quiet after boot.

This change was made with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude).

Fixes: 5b6b6ef36ff2 ("stmmac/dwmac-sun60i: snps,dwmac-5.20 compat + EXT gmii clock + PHY reset - MDIO was reading wrong core type (DWMAC100 vs real GMAC4, Synopsys 0x53) dts/opi4pro: drop init=/bin/sh, restore normal sysvinit/OpenRC boot")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/clk/clk.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/clk.c b/drivers/clk/clk.c
index 5eff0ca3c..0f06254c7 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/clk.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk.c
@@ -1253,7 +1253,7 @@ int clk_pcie_watch(const char *cmd, const char *name);
 
 int clk_pcie_watch(const char *cmd, const char *name)
 {
-	pr_emerg("a733-clk: %s %s\n", cmd, name);
+	pr_debug("a733-clk: %s %s\n", cmd, name);
 	return 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(clk_pcie_watch);
